### Content summary

Anchored to the principle: *“Does the theme reinforce brand temperament without fighting content?”* (accent usage; dark/light balance).

- **Purpose** — PDCA framing; Forge theme packs (`forge-theme.css`, `forgesdlc-theme.css`, `docs-theme.css`); amber/cyan role system vs deterministic token/font/contrast rules.
- **Passing / failing signals** — Accent role stability, dark foundation, focal `forge-gradient-text`, theme-pack consistency, ambient restraint, typography calm; failures include accent roulette, gradient overload, light/dark whiplash, Bootstrap drift.
- **Before example** — Failing HTML: inline hex, `btn-success`/`btn-warning`/`btn-info`, multi-line `forge-gradient-text`, `bg-light` band, `card border-info`, purple inline borders.
- **After example** — Passing HTML from `components/components.py` / `layouts.py` patterns: `landing-hero fs-landing-hero-band`, `landing-hero-kicker`, `product-landing-title`, `btn-forge` + `btn-cyan-outline`, `forge-card card-amber breathe-link`, `glass breathe-static`, hash markers.
- **Evidence and remediation** — 7-step ordered fix list ending with AI re-run + deterministic companion proposal.
- **Related rules** — Corrected `AI.VISUAL.HIERARCHY` (registry ID; old page had non-registry `AI.VISUAL.HIERARCHY_CONFIDENCE`).

